# Files excluded from the expo-updates fingerprint (runtimeVersion policy).
#
# EAS Build runs `pod install` BEFORE the CONFIGURE_EXPO_UPDATES phase computes
# the fingerprint. CocoaPods rewrites both of these files on every run --
# project.pbxproj gets freshly generated random 24-hex UUIDs for every Pods file
# reference, and Podfile.lock records the CocoaPods version that produced it.
# Because ios/ is committed to this repo, that churn made the iOS runtime version
# differ between this machine and EAS on every single build, which fails the
# build outright. Android has no equivalent step and always matched.
#
# Excluding them is safe: genuine native changes are still captured by the other
# fingerprint sources -- the resolved Expo config, config plugins, and the
# autolinked native module directories under node_modules.
ios/Podfile.lock
ios/**/project.pbxproj
